## Tasks

### Task 1 — Hit All 3 Endpoints and Verify Response Shapes

**What:** Before writing ANY code, authenticate and hit all 3 endpoints. Capture actual response shapes.

```bash
# Login as Tenant Owner
TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth/login \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"email":"contact@honeydo4you.com","password":"978@F32c"}' | grep -o '"access_token":"[^"]*"' | cut -d'"' -f4)

# 1. GET /time-clock/reports/timesheet
curl -s "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/time-clock/reports/timesheet?date_from=2026-01-01&date_to=2026-04-10" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" | head -c 5000

# 2. GET /time-clock/reports/payroll
curl -s "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/time-clock/reports/payroll?date_from=2026-01-01&date_to=2026-04-10" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" | head -c 5000

# 3. GET /time-clock/reports/payroll/export (CSV — check Content-Type header)
curl -s -D - "http://localhost:8000/api/v1/time-clock/reports/payroll/export?date_from=2026-01-01&date_to=2026-04-10" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" | head -c 2000
```

**Acceptance:** All 3 response shapes captured. Types created or updated in `app/src/lib/types/time-clock.ts`.
**Do NOT:** Skip this step. Do NOT guess response shapes.

